# A click on a row of the panel means the line of its output that is there, not the
# line of the window: the program prints a place in a file at its twentieth line, the
# panel is following the end (top 13), and the row at y = 442 + 22 * 6 = 574 is that line,
# which is where the click goes.
# files at.cm=class Main from IO\n  def main:\n    Int i = 1\n    while i < 19:\n      out("line ${i}\\n")\n      i = i + 1\n    end\n    out("at.cm | Line : 3 | Column : 5 | Error: here\\n")\n  end\nend\n
# open at.cm
# args --catmintc @ROOT@/catmintc
# frames 6
# expect cursor 3 5
1 key f5
2 wait idle
3 click 100 574
